
 logarch - Archive RDA log files to the DECSDATA area.

 Safe to run at any time: log files that are already archived are
 detected and skipped (unless -n is given).

 USAGE:
   logarch [-b] [-n] [-s] [-c CcAddress] [-p LogPath] [-m YearMonth]
           (-a | -d | -o | -t | -w) [more archive-type flags]

 ARCHIVE TYPES (at least one required):

   -a   Archive AWS log files.
   -d   Archive dssdb log files.
   -o   Archive OSDF log files.
   -t   Archive THREDDS log files.
   -w   Archive Web log files.

 OPTIONAL FLAGS:

   -m YearMonth
        Archive logs for the given YYYY-MM (e.g. 2024-01) only.

   -c CcAddress
        Carbon-copy the email notice to one or more additional specialists
        (comma/space-separated). May be given more than once.

   -p LogPath
        Use LogPath instead of the default log directory.

   -s   Append PBS sublog files to the common log files.

   -n   Skip the "already-archived" check (force re-archive).

   -b   Run in background mode (log to file only, no terminal output).

 EXAMPLE:
   logarch -w -m 2024-01
